Description: Fix CVE-2026-32775: integer underflow in MakerNote entries
Author: Deepin CI Robot <packages@deepin.org>
Origin: upstream
Bug: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-32775
Forwarded: not-needed
---
This patch fixes an integer underflow vulnerability in the MakerNote entry
processing functions by adding a bounds check before any string operations.

The vulnerability occurred when maxlen was 0, causing maxlen-- to underflow
and potentially leading to buffer overflow issues.

Index: github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775/libexif/apple/mnote-apple-entry.c
===================================================================
--- github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775.orig/libexif/apple/mnote-apple-entry.c
+++ github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775/libexif/apple/mnote-apple-entry.c
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ mnote_apple_entry_get_value(MnoteAppleEn
     if (!entry)
         return NULL;
 
+	if (maxlen < 1)
+		return NULL;
+
     memset(v, 0, maxlen);
     maxlen--;
 
Index: github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775/libexif/canon/mnote-canon-entry.c
===================================================================
--- github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775.orig/libexif/canon/mnote-canon-entry.c
+++ github-libexif-CVE-2026-32775/libexif/canon/mnote-canon-entry.c
@@ -562,6 +562,9 @@ mnote_canon_entry_get_value (const Mnote
 	if (!entry) 
 		return NULL;
 
+	if (maxlen < 1)
+		return NULL;
+
 	data = entry->data;
 	size = entry->size;
 
